  "notes": "The model reproduces the 770 m curved crest road, fourteen ribbed overflow openings, four south-flank radial gates with distinct chutes, and six recessed lower outlet openings. The signed crest follows the retained access roads at both abutments. The Earth viewer uses separate 1170.5 m reservoir and 1106 m tailwater surfaces. The four radial chute runs and the two southern outlet recesses sit above the fitted terrain. Both access roads meet the modeled deck at 1180 m at the sampled joins. The tailwater and local bank grades are representative exterior estimates. The outer banks retain some sharp edges at coarse terrain resolution. Operating discharge and the underground generating station are outside the model. The host supplies the matching Protomaps feature IDs and terrain samples fine enough to resolve the graded shoulders.",
